<https://w3id.org/dpv#ConsentStatus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "States are useful as information artefacts to implement them in controlling processing, and to reflect the process and flow of obtaining and maintaining consent. For example, a database table that stores consent states for specific processing and can be queried to obtain them in an efficient manner. States are also useful in investigations to determine the use and validity of consenting practices"@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
