<https://w3id.org/dpv#IdentifyingPersonalData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "DPV does not use PII ('Personally Identifiable Information') as it has varying and conflicting definitions across sources. Instead the concept 'identifying personal data' is intended to provide a clear categorisation of its interpretation. Where multiple data categories can be combined to create an 'identifying' category e.g. fingerprinting, this concept represents the combined category."@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
