<https://w3id.org/dpv#LegalBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Legal basis used to justify processing of data or use of technology in accordance with a law"@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#LegalBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/dpv#legal-basis-classes> <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#LegalBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Legal Basis"@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#LegalBasis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Legal basis (plural: legal bases) are defined by legislations and regulations, whose applicability is usually restricted to specific jurisdictions which can be represented using dpv:hasJurisdiction or dpv:hasLaw. Legal basis can be used without such declarations, e.g. 'Consent', however their interpretation will require association with a law, e.g. 'EU GDPR'."@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#LegalCompliance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Georg P. Krog, Harshvardhan J. Pandit, Beatriz Esteves" <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#LegalCompliance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
