<https://w3id.org/dpv#NonPersonalData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The term NonPersonalData is provided to distinguish between PersonalData and other data, e.g. for indicating which data is regulated by privacy laws. To specify personal data that has been anonymised, the concept AnonymisedData should be used as the anonymisation process has a risk of not being fully effective and such anonymous data may be found to be personal data depending on circumstances."@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
