<https://w3id.org/dpv#SensitivePersonalData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Personal data that is considered 'sensitive' in terms of privacy and/or impact, and therefore requires additional considerations and/or protection"@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#SensitivePersonalData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/dpv#personal-data-classes> <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#SensitivePersonalData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Sensitive Personal Data"@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
<https://w3id.org/dpv#SensitivePersonalData> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Sensitivity' is a matter of context, and may be defined within legal frameworks. For GDPR, Special categories of personal data are considered a subset of sensitive data. To illustrate the difference between the two, consider the situation where Location data is collected, and which is considered 'sensitive' but not 'special'. As a probable rule, sensitive data require additional considerations whereas special category data requires additional legal basis / justifications."@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
