<https://w3id.org/dpv#SensitivityLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "ISO/IEC TS 38505-3:2021 defines 'data sensitivity' as the potential harm of unauthorised disclosure. DPV's use of the concept goes beyond disclosure as it refers to the level of safeguards or controls the data requires as a reflection of its 'sensitive' nature. To indicate quantified levels of sensitivity, e.g. \"high sensitivity\", instances of severity can be directly used or specialised"@en <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
